          "text": "**Analyzing ramp dynamics**\n\nI\u2019m calculating how the 7 degrees of incline and gravity work together on a ramp. I found that the total energy adjusts and might allow the ball to stop on the ramp. Before the ramp, the speed fluctuates between 0.98 and 0.96, and there's energy loss during ascent. The friction factor is critical here; adjustments for low rolling resistance are essential. Overlaps with the cup\u2019s base may affect collisions. Overall, the ramp design seems feasible with minimal energy impact.",
